From 6146edbd8ac30daabbadcf8138e8ea1a41f49495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MATIAS <mnpn31@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:59:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Preliminary support for the `Kundt Tube` experiment type.

Same eight-file shape as `Electron Diffraction` (4a27491): migration, Prisma
model, DTO, channel, @EventPattern, handler, service read/write and the
GET/POST/@Sse endpoints.

Three things are specific to this experiment:

The tube has three independent ESP32 modules (audio generation, microphone,
motorised plunger) that share platform_id and controller_id and are told apart
by which fields they publish. One logical controller keeps the experiment state
in a single row.

Every DTO field is optional and the handler merges instead of replacing, since
writing `undefined` into a Prisma update leaves the column untouched. Without
this the microphone module blanks out whatever the plunger module just
reported. Verified against three real boards.

Routes use :id rather than :platform_id, because ValidReservationGuard reads
request.params.id and any route declaring :platform_id is rejected with 403.
